    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the problem is the \"smaller system\" thing doesn't work. the math doesn't reset just because you change the scale. if the core variables are broken, any output is just more noise. it feels less like a setback and more like a fundamental flaw in the system's architecture. like, if the trajectory is a downward curve that's already passed the point of no return, isn't trying to build something new just ignoring the actual data?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
